{% comment %}
  Rebrand class hero — the head of a single class page: a teal class-type
  line, the subject in coral IvyPresto italic, "With <teacher>" in roman
  below it, a row of icon facts and a coral Book Now pill. One colour picture
  fills the box beside it; "media_mode" can restore the comp's pair of images,
  which run off the right edge with the second in black and white.

  Everything defaults out of the booking metafields this store already keeps
  on class products, so a class page is correct the moment it is assigned the
  template:

    booking.class_type        eyebrow          ("Annual Class")
    booking.instructor_name   "With <name>"
    booking.class_time        clock fact       ("10am-12pm")
    booking.skill_level       level fact       ("Beginner - Intermediate")
    booking.capacity          group-size fact  ("16 Max")

  Every one of them can still be overridden in the editor, and the section
  works on a page template too — it just needs the fields filled in by hand.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'saf-rebrand.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign sid = section.id
  assign p = product

  assign eyebrow = section.settings.eyebrow
  if eyebrow == blank
    assign eyebrow = p.metafields.booking.class_type
  endif

  assign teacher = section.settings.teacher
  if teacher == blank
    assign teacher = p.metafields.booking.instructor_name
  endif

  comment
    The comp splits the class into a subject ("Watercolour") and a teacher line
    ("With Kerry Sassen"), but this store names class products with both in one
    string — "WATERCOLOUR WITH KERRI SASSEN". Printing the whole title as the
    subject says the teacher's name twice, so the trailing "with <teacher>" is
    trimmed off. Liquid's split is case sensitive and the catalog is not
    consistent about case, so the separator is normalised first.
  endcomment
  assign title = section.settings.title
  if title == blank
    assign title = p.title
    if section.settings.strip_teacher
      assign normalised = title | replace: ' WITH ', ' with ' | replace: ' With ', ' with '
      assign title = normalised | split: ' with ' | first
    endif
  endif

  assign fact_time = section.settings.fact_time
  if fact_time == blank
    assign fact_time = p.metafields.booking.class_time
  endif

  assign fact_level = section.settings.fact_level
  if fact_level == blank
    assign fact_level = p.metafields.booking.skill_level
  endif

  assign fact_size = section.settings.fact_size
  if fact_size == blank
    assign cap = p.metafields.booking.capacity
    if cap != blank
      assign fact_size = cap | append: ' Max'
    endif
  endif

  comment
    2026-09-12: the class page picture can now be chosen per class from the
    booking app's Class tab, separately from the grid card photo, so a class
    can lead its own page with one shot and the Classes grid with another.

      booking.hero_image   this picture      (blank = the class's main photo)
      booking.hero_focal   top|middle|bottom (blank = the tuned default below)

    The editor setting still wins, so a hand-placed image on one page is never
    overwritten by the app.
  endcomment
  assign img_a = section.settings.image_a | default: p.metafields.booking.hero_image.value | default: p.featured_image

  assign focal_y = section.settings.photo_focal_y
  assign focal_pick = p.metafields.booking.hero_focal.value | downcase | strip
  case focal_pick
    when 'top'
      assign focal_y = 0
    when 'middle'
      assign focal_y = 50
    when 'bottom'
      assign focal_y = 100
  endcase
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The second image is the teacher's portrait. One template serves every class,
  so it has to follow the class's own teacher rather than be picked per page.
  Same lookup the teacher band uses — see snippets/rb-teacher-handle.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture rb_teacher_handle -%}{%- render 'rb-teacher-handle', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img_b = section.settings.image_b
  if img_b == blank
    assign teacher_handle = rb_teacher_handle | strip
    if teacher_handle != blank
      assign img_b = collections[teacher_handle].image
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  2026-09-10, client: the class hero "needs to be one colour image". The pair
  reads as a colour photo with a grey square stuck to it — the same note the
  artist pages got, answered the same way (see media_mode on rb-person-hero and
  rb-artist-cards): one picture, in colour, filling the box.

  Kept as a setting rather than a deletion so Hanre's two-image comp is one
  click away.

  In single mode the class's own photo is the picture; a class with no photo of
  its own falls back to its teacher's, rather than showing an empty box.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign show_portrait = false
  if section.settings.media_mode == 'pair' and img_b != blank
    assign show_portrait = true
  endif
  if show_portrait == false and img_a == blank
    assign img_a = img_b
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  2026-09-11: when the class's teacher has a gallery, the picture opens it
  full-screen (same viewer as the page nav's "Gallery" link — see
  snippets/rb-gallery.liquid). No gallery, no change: the picture stays a
  plain picture.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture rb_gal -%}{%- render 'rb-gallery', product: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}

<style>
  {% comment %}
    The picture is the person hero's box, not this comp's — same width, same
    height, flush with the top of the section (client instruction 2026-08-30;
    see --rb-hero-* in saf-rebrand.css). Two consequences worth knowing:

    the media track is a PERCENTAGE OF THE ROW rather than a fr share, because
    a fr share is measured after the gap is taken out and would land 79px
    short of the person hero's picture; and the section lost its vertical
    padding, because the picture — now taller than the copy beside it — sets
    the height, exactly as it does on a person page.
  {% endcomment %}
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch {
    background: {{ section.settings.background }};
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr {{ 100 | minus: section.settings.text_width }}%;
    align-items: center;
    /* shared with the person hero — see --rb-hero-* in saf-rebrand.css */
    gap: var(--rb-hero-gap);
    padding-block: 0;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__text {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding-inline: var(--rb-gutter) 0;
    /* keep the copy on the same measure as every other container on the site
       rather than letting it run the full half-width */
    max-width: calc(var(--rb-container) / 2 + var(--rb-gutter));
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__eyebrow { margin-bottom: clamp(4px, 0.42vw, 8px); }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__title {
    color: {{ section.settings.title_color }};
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__teacher {
    color: {{ section.settings.teacher_color }};
    margin-top: -0.06em; /* the two lines nearly touch in the comp */
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__facts {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(12px, 1.72vw, 33px);
    margin-top: clamp(10px, 1.15vw, 22px);
    color: {{ section.settings.fact_color }};
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__fact {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(5px, 0.42vw, 8px);
    font-family: var(--rb-sans);
    font-size: var(--rb-fs-body-sm);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__fact svg {
    width: clamp(14px, 1.04vw, 20px);
    height: clamp(14px, 1.04vw, 20px);
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__cta {
    margin-top: clamp(16px, 1.98vw, 38px);
    min-height: clamp(36px, 2.5vw, 48px);
  }

  /* the pair of images bleeds off the right edge, cropping the second */
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(4px, 0.42vw, 8px);
    overflow: hidden;
    height: var(--rb-hero-media-h);
  }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media { height: 100%; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media[data-rb-gallery-open] { cursor: zoom-in; }
  #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media[data-rb-gallery-open]:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid {{ section.settings.teacher_color }};
    outline-offset: -4px;
  }
  {%- if show_portrait -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media { flex: 0 0 {{ section.settings.image_a_width }}%; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media--b { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 60%; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media--b img { filter: grayscale(1); }
  {%- else -%}
    {% comment %}
      One picture, so it fills the box instead of bleeding off the edge. Class
      photos are upright (1080x1350 on every live class) and this box is wide,
      so a centred crop takes the head off — same focal-point fix, and the same
      35% default, as the artist hero and the artist index cards.

      booking.hero_focal overrides that default per class (see focal_y above),
      which is how the booking app's top/middle/bottom choice reaches the page.
    {% endcomment %}
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media { flex: 1 1 100%; }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media .rb-media img {
      object-position: {{ section.settings.photo_focal_x }}% {{ focal_y }}%;
    }
  {%- endif -%}

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-block: 40px 0;
    }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__text {
      max-width: none;
      margin-left: 0;
      padding-inline: var(--rb-gutter);
    }
    #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media { height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; }
    {%- unless show_portrait -%}
      {% comment %}
        16/9 is right for a cropped pair; a person standing up survives an
        upright box far better, and on one narrow column there is room for it.
      {% endcomment %}
      #shopify-section-{{ sid }} .rb-ch__media { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; }
    {%- endunless -%}
  }
</style>

<div class="rb-section rb-bleed">
  <div class="rb-ch">
    <div class="rb-ch__text">
      {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="rb-caps rb-ch__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if title != blank -%}
        <h1 class="rb-name rb-name--lg rb-ch__title">{{ title }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if teacher != blank -%}
        <p class="rb-name rb-name--lg rb-ch__teacher">
          {{- section.settings.teacher_prefix }} {{ teacher -}}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if fact_time != blank or fact_level != blank or fact_size != blank -%}
        <ul class="rb-ch__facts" role="list">
          {%- if fact_time != blank -%}
            <li class="rb-ch__fact">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 7v5l3.5 2"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>{{ fact_time }}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if fact_level != blank -%}
            <li class="rb-ch__fact">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 12l4-3"></path><path d="M7.5 15.5h9"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>{{ fact_level }}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if fact_size != blank -%}
            <li class="rb-ch__fact">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="3.4"></circle><path d="M5.5 19.5a6.5 6.5 0 0 1 13 0"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>{{ fact_size }}</span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.button_label != blank -%}
        <a
          href="{{ section.settings.button_link | default: '#rb-book' }}"
          class="rb-btn rb-btn--serif rb-btn--coral rb-ch__cta"
        >{{ section.settings.button_label | escape }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div
      class="rb-ch__media"
      {%- if rb_gal != blank %}
        data-rb-gallery-open
        role="button"
        tabindex="0"
        aria-haspopup="dialog"
        aria-label="Open the gallery{% if teacher != blank %} of {{ teacher | escape }}’s work{% endif %}"
      {%- endif %}
    >
      <div class="rb-media">
        {%- if img_a != blank -%}
          {%- if show_portrait -%}
            {%- assign img_a_sizes = '(max-width: 749px) 100vw, 33vw' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign img_a_sizes = '(max-width: 749px) 100vw, 52vw' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {{
            img_a
            | image_url: width: 1600
            | image_tag: widths: '400, 600, 900, 1200, 1600', sizes: img_a_sizes,
              loading: 'eager', alt: img_a.alt | default: title
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if show_portrait -%}
        <div class="rb-media rb-media--b">
          {{
            img_b
            | image_url: width: 1400
            | image_tag: widths: '300, 500, 700, 900, 1400', sizes: '(max-width: 749px) 60vw, 32vw',
              loading: 'eager', alt: img_b.alt | default: teacher
          }}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{{- rb_gal -}}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Rebrand class hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "rb-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Leave the text fields blank on a class product page and each one fills itself from that product's booking metafields." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Class type",
      "info": "Blank uses booking.class_type." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Subject",
      "info": "Blank uses the product title." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "strip_teacher", "default": true,
      "label": "Trim \"with <teacher>\" off the product title",
      "info": "Class products here are named \"Watercolour with Kerri Sassen\"; the design shows the subject and the teacher on separate lines." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "teacher_prefix", "default": "With", "label": "Teacher prefix" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "teacher", "label": "Teacher",
      "info": "Blank uses booking.instructor_name." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Facts" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_time", "label": "Time",
      "info": "Blank uses booking.class_time." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_level", "label": "Level",
      "info": "Blank uses booking.skill_level." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fact_size", "label": "Group size",
      "info": "Blank uses booking.capacity." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Button" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "default": "Book Now", "label": "Button label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button_link", "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Blank jumps to the booking widget further down the page." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Images" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_mode", "label": "What the picture shows", "default": "single",
      "options": [
        { "value": "single", "label": "One colour image" },
        { "value": "pair", "label": "Class image with the teacher's photo beside it" }
      ],
      "info": "Class pages use one colour image. The pair is Hanre's original design — the teacher's photo runs off the right edge in black and white." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image_a", "label": "Class image",
      "info": "Blank uses the picture chosen in the booking app's Class tab, then the product's featured image, then the teacher's photo if the class has none." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "photo_focal_x", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 50, "unit": "%", "label": "Focal point — horizontal" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "photo_focal_y", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 35, "unit": "%", "label": "Focal point — vertical",
      "info": "An upright photo is cropped into a wide box. Lower numbers keep the head." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image_b", "label": "Teacher portrait",
      "info": "Only used by the pair. Blank uses the picture on this class's teacher collection." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "image_a_width", "min": 30, "max": 100, "step": 1,
      "default": 62, "unit": "%", "label": "Class image share of the pair" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "text_width", "min": 30, "max": 70, "step": 1,
      "default": 48, "unit": "%", "label": "Text share of the row",
      "info": "The picture takes the rest of the row and the copy sits in what is left of it, less a gutter. Artist and teacher pages are set to the same 48, so changing it here parts the class hero from those." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "default": "#ffffff", "label": "Background" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "title_color", "default": "#e07468", "label": "Subject colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "teacher_color", "default": "#1e1e1e", "label": "Teacher line colour" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "fact_color", "default": "#1e1e1e", "label": "Facts colour" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Rebrand class hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
